{# Standalone `free` model group (2026-09-22 operator decision). Split out of
   model-list.yaml.j2 when that file crossed its per-file token budget,
   following the seam that file already uses for every other tier: one group
   per file, so an agent changing this one reads this file and not every
   other tier as well. Per .token-limits.yaml the remedy for an over-budget
   file is a split along a real seam, never a raised budget.

   Included by model-list.yaml.j2, which owns the macros and the surrounding
   tiers; `litellm_model` resolves from that context.

   A caller-facing group no chain segment feeds into: every registry entry
   marked `free: true` (llm-models.d/40-hermes-cloud.yml,
   llm-models.d/50-openrouter.yml) gets a SECOND deployment here under this
   one shared model_name, load-balanced by LiteLLM's own Router the same
   way any other multi-deployment group already is (hermes-cloud-openrouter's
   kimi/glm pair, model-list.yaml.j2's hermes-cloud loop). Its own ladder
   registration — route_group for a hermes-cloud entry, client_model_id for
   an openrouter one — is untouched, so this is an ADDITIONAL registration
   of the same entry, never a duplicated fact. config.yaml.j2's
   cross-modality fail-fast loop gives `free` its own explicit empty
   fallbacks/context_window_fallbacks entry, so a busy/failed call under
   this name fails fast rather than reaching for a chain segment this group
   was never part of.

   `order`, ranked widest-context-first: LiteLLM's own order filtering keeps
   only the lowest-order deployment(s) among healthy siblings
   (assert-registry-render-parity.yml's NARROW-DEPLOYMENT-PREFERRED check),
   so an unranked group would let whichever member happens to sort first
   capture every request under this name — including one only a wider
   sibling could serve — and silently truncate or refuse it. #}
{% for m in llm_router_registry_enabled | selectattr('free', 'defined') | selectattr('free')
     | sort(attribute='context_window', reverse=true) %}
{% set _free_key = llm_router_resolved_credentials.get(m.credential_env, '') %}
{% if _free_key | length > 0 %}
  - model_name: free
    litellm_params:
      model: {{ litellm_model(m) }}
      api_key: os.environ/{{ m.credential_env }}
      use_chat_completions_api: true
      order: {{ loop.index0 }}
      # Every current free-marked entry shares OPENROUTER_API_KEY, the same
      # account-wide credential 30-openrouter.yml's own rate ceilings
      # already protect — reused here rather than a second set of numbers
      # for the same key. The only enforcement a storage-less proxy has on
      # an account-wide credential (test_openrouter_allowlist.yml).
      rpm: {{ llm_router_openrouter_rpm }}
      tpm: {{ llm_router_openrouter_tpm }}
      max_parallel_requests: {{ llm_router_openrouter_max_parallel_requests }}
    model_info:
      disable_background_health_check: true
      max_input_tokens: {{ m.context_window }}
{% if m.max_output_tokens is defined %}
      max_output_tokens: {{ m.max_output_tokens }}
      max_tokens: {{ m.max_output_tokens }}
{% else %}
      max_tokens: {{ m.context_window }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
